WEBVTT

00:00.400 --> 00:02.664
Data pipelines are rarely one tool.

00:02.815 --> 00:05.659
They're models, scripts, brokers and databases,

00:05.810 --> 00:07.378
scattered across machines.

00:07.819 --> 00:12.707
The DataCROP Workflow Management Editor brings them onto one canvas.

00:13.533 --> 00:14.752
The idea is simple.

00:14.926 --> 00:18.014
Every processing component, a machine-learning model,

00:18.131 --> 00:21.056
an LLM service, a plain Python script,

00:21.230 --> 00:24.203
becomes a black box: a processor definition.

00:24.644 --> 00:26.118
It declares how it runs,

00:26.234 --> 00:28.277
which data it accepts and produces,

00:28.428 --> 00:31.783
and the settings it needs as environment variables.

00:32.600 --> 00:34.214
Bring code you already have:

00:34.655 --> 00:37.383
a container image for a single-container deployment,

00:37.557 --> 00:40.739
or a GitHub repository with a Docker Compose application.

00:41.342 --> 00:43.711
WME provisions it onto every worker,

00:43.838 --> 00:45.185
ready to run.

00:46.000 --> 00:47.823
Data sources are modelled too.

00:48.252 --> 00:51.317
Choose an interface: Kafka, Elasticsearch,

00:51.468 --> 00:56.472
MQTT, MongoDB, S3, Redis, RabbitMQ,

00:56.623 --> 00:58.260
HTTP or Beats.

00:58.748 --> 01:00.327
Fill in its connection details,

01:00.385 --> 01:04.297
and attach a data kind that describes the payload and its schema.

01:05.099 --> 01:06.226
Then you compose.

01:06.505 --> 01:10.116
Drag processors and resources onto the canvas and connect them.

01:10.557 --> 01:13.030
The editor only allows compatible links.

01:13.633 --> 01:15.839
Pick the worker each processor runs on,

01:15.967 --> 01:20.704
set its parameters, and every connected resource is injected automatically as extra

01:20.762 --> 01:22.793
environment variables.

01:23.600 --> 01:27.780
Save, and WME generates an Apache Airflow DAG for the workflow,

01:28.058 --> 01:30.125
plus a teardown DAG to stop it.

01:30.566 --> 01:33.492
Each processor is routed to its worker's Celery queue,

01:33.619 --> 01:37.532
where a lightweight agent starts it with Docker Compose or Docker run.

01:38.136 --> 01:39.680
Run once or on a schedule,

01:39.796 --> 01:42.129
across as many workers as you need.

01:42.933 --> 01:45.069
Some jobs need no custom code.

01:45.510 --> 01:50.619
The built-in Logstash processor turns connected sources into a continuous pipeline:

01:51.002 --> 01:55.042
inputs in, outputs out, with an optional filter in between.

01:55.553 --> 01:57.504
And the Logstash assistant can draft,

01:57.550 --> 02:00.302
explain or fix that filter for you.

02:01.133 --> 02:03.432
To see what actually flows through your system,

02:03.548 --> 02:04.895
create observations.

02:05.336 --> 02:08.923
One click adds a pipeline that tags every event with its source,

02:09.132 --> 02:11.559
asset, data kind and timestamp,

02:11.710 --> 02:14.508
and indexes it into Elasticsearch.

02:15.333 --> 02:18.665
Any Elasticsearch resource opens straight into Kibana,

02:18.816 --> 02:23.506
where WME builds the data view and a ready-made dashboard for you.

02:24.333 --> 02:28.675
Once running, the Worker Runtime view shows every deployed container across your

02:28.733 --> 02:29.337
workers.

02:29.778 --> 02:31.984
Check health, read logs, and start,

02:32.077 --> 02:36.617
stop or restart processors, while Airflow run history and the pipeline monitor

02:36.651 --> 02:38.405
track every deployment.

02:39.233 --> 02:40.487
Or skip the clicking.

02:40.928 --> 02:43.413
Describe what you need to the Workflow Assistant.

02:43.854 --> 02:47.871
It searches your catalogue, creates missing data kinds and resources,

02:48.254 --> 02:49.775
checks which workers are ready,

02:49.891 --> 02:52.062
and assembles a complete workflow draft,

02:52.085 --> 02:54.790
for you to inspect in the Lab and run.

02:55.600 --> 02:56.889
Model your components.

02:57.005 --> 02:58.154
Describe your data.

02:58.328 --> 03:01.927
Connect, deploy and observe, by hand or with AI.

03:02.531 --> 03:05.167
DataCROP Workflow Management Editor.
